      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear that you feel more comfortable exploring further options at home, but I'd strongly advise against putting butter or any other forms of oil or fat directly onto the burn. This can actually trap heat and exacerbate the injury. The richer blood supply in certain areas of the skin, like on the forearm or behind the elbow, can make burns even worse when you apply such substances. If possible, seek any medical help or consider using sterile burn cream or an over-the-counter burn relief product, as these are designed for such situations. Remember, burns should be treated immediately and appropriately to prevent infection and promote healing.",
