      "content": "Attempting to drain blisters yourself without medical training or sterile conditions can lead to infections or worsen the situation. Blisters serve as a protective barrier against infection. If you feel the need to relieve pressure or reduce discomfort, it's better to consult with a healthcare professional even if it's just over the phone. Remember, human skin has natural mechanisms to protect wounds, and unnecessary interference can be bad. If possible, keep the burn and blisters covered with sterile, non-fluffy dressings and use cool, clean, moist compresses every few hours. Proper wound care can prevent infection and aid in faster healing. If the burn or blister appears to be severe or if there are signs of infection, it's crucial to seek medical attention.",
